<title>JAPAN: IBJ says leaving March prime rate unchanged.</title>
<headline>IBJ says leaving March prime rate unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd (IBJ) said on Monday it would leave its long-term prime lending rate for March unchanged at 2.5 percent, a record low.</p>
<p>The long-term prime lending rate, applied to loans of one year and longer to the bank's most creditworthy clients, was last cut in December to 2.5 percent from 2.7 percent in November.</p>
</text>
